; Part of ferrum. MIT licence, see ferrum/LICENSE.
; FIND skew: o<probe_edge_skew> call [axis] [side] [d1] [d2]. Measures how
; far an edge of the part is turned from the machine's axes from two
; touches at chosen places along it, and with #3030 = 0 sets the active
; work system's rotation to match, so its X (or Y) runs along the edge.
; Nothing else is written: the rotation turns about the work origin as it
; is, so probe the corner (X0 Y0) first and the skew after.
; [axis] 0 for the left/right edge (touches along X, the edge runs in Y),
; 1 for the front/back edge (touches along Y, the edge runs in X); [side]
; -1 for left/front, +1 for right/back. [d1] and [d2] are where the two
; touches go along the edge, measured from the start in the direction of
; +Y (left/right) or +X (front/back), in machine units, at least #3019
; apart. The probe starts above the top, less than step-off #3023 in from
; the edge.
;   1. With #3030 = 0 the rotation is cleared first, so the angle is
;      measured in machine-aligned axes.
;   2. Top touch at the start -> top (z_minus_probed_position #1009).
;   3. Guarded move #3023 off the edge, guarded plunge #3021 + tip
;      diameter #5410 + #3022, guarded move to [d1]; edge touch towards
;      the part. Guarded move to [d2]; edge touch.
;   4. angle = the edge's turn from the axis, degrees, counter-clockwise
;      positive seen from above. Reports edge_delta #1011 (how far the
;      edge moves across, second touch minus first) and edge_angle #1012.
;   5. Guarded rise; guarded move back over the start.
;   6. With #3030 = 0: G10 L2 R<angle> on the active work system.
o<probe_edge_skew> sub
o10 if [#<_task> EQ 0]
    o<probe_edge_skew> return
o10 endif
#<axis> = #1
#<side> = #2
#<d1> = #3
#<d2> = #4
o100 if [[#<axis> NE 0] AND [#<axis> NE 1]]
    (ABORT, Skew axis must be 0 or 1)
o100 endif
o110 if [ABS[#<side>] NE 1]
    (ABORT, Skew side must be 1 or -1)
o110 endif
o120 if [#3023 LE 0]
    (ABORT, Probe step-off width must be positive)
o120 endif
o130 if [ABS[#<d2> - #<d1>] LT #3019]
    (ABORT, Put the two touches further apart along the edge than the XY clearance)
o130 endif
#<rotate> = [#3030 EQ 0]
o<ferrum_probe_ready> call [#<rotate>]
M73
M50 P0
G90 G94
o140 if [#<rotate>]
    G10 L2 P0 R0
o140 endif

; u across the edge (probing axis), v along it.
#<ux> = [#<axis> EQ 0]
#<uy> = [#<axis> EQ 1]
#<z_stack> = [#3021 + #5410 + #3022]
#<u_start> = #[5420 + #<axis>]
#<v_start> = #[5421 - #<axis>]

o<ferrum_top> call [#3020]
#<top> = #<_ferrum_top>

o<ferrum_guarded_move> call [#<ux> * #<side> * #3023] [#<uy> * #<side> * #3023] [0]
o<ferrum_guarded_move> call [0] [0] [0 - #<z_stack>]
o<ferrum_guarded_move> call [#<uy> * #<d1>] [#<ux> * #<d1>] [0]
o<ferrum_edge> call [#<axis>] [0 - #<side>] [#3018]
#<e1> = #<_ferrum_edge>
o<ferrum_guarded_move> call [#<uy> * [#<v_start> + #<d2> - #5420]] [#<ux> * [#<v_start> + #<d2> - #5421]] [0]
o<ferrum_edge> call [#<axis>] [0 - #<side>] [#3018]
#<e2> = #<_ferrum_edge>

; Left/right: a part turned counter-clockwise has its edge's X fall as Y
; rises. Front/back: its edge's Y rises with X.
#<delta> = [#<e2> - #<e1>]
o150 if [#<axis> EQ 0]
    #<angle> = [ATAN[0 - #<delta>] / [#<d2> - #<d1>]]
o150 else
    #<angle> = [ATAN[#<delta>] / [#<d2> - #<d1>]]
o150 endif
; ATAN[y]/[x] is atan2: a negative run gives the angle beyond 90 degrees.
o160 if [#<angle> GT 90]
    #<angle> = [#<angle> - 180]
o160 elseif [#<angle> LT -90]
    #<angle> = [#<angle> + 180]
o160 endif
#1011 = #<delta>
#1012 = #<angle>
(DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"edge_delta"}.setValue{#<delta>}])
(DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"edge_angle"}.setValue{#<angle>}])

o<ferrum_guarded_move> call [0] [0] [#<z_stack>]
o<ferrum_guarded_move> call [#<ux> * [#<u_start> - #5420] + #<uy> * [#<v_start> - #5420]] [#<uy> * [#<u_start> - #5421] + #<ux> * [#<v_start> - #5421]] [0]
o200 if [#<rotate>]
    G10 L2 P0 R#<angle>
o200 endif
G90
o<probe_edge_skew> endsub
M2
